icit nonmultipartite equality examples and L1-close tying paths, and the complete rank-one latent-product profile strictly below the achievable source construction at every interior density. None supplies the missing all-host comparison.\n\nAcceptance follows source-first root reconstruction, three independent reviews across distinct mechanisms, a new whole-package adversarial audit, and independent reproduction of complete stored outputs. All 93,505 author assertions and 1,080 historical review assertions replay exactly. Fresh independent universal proofs and controls supplement those finite checks. Five fresh pinned primary PDFs were read and revalidated separately; portable wrappers do not fetch sources. No novelty certification is claimed.\n\nOriginal head: c683fc4b84266a6a153c087e182cf427ed502d6c. Author checkpoint: e27668a5dd99e38705ec6a97d15710b7eb1b0f41. Queue-only refreshed head: 26df33899c95d860403ab311c568e0328bc87eeb, with current-main parent ceada39994b1cd2c4935709143b53e2f7a581a45. All 45 original mathematical/review/publication files remain byte-identical; only this problem's queue status and turn count change against that parent. Historical pending-review statements remain frozen history, with the accepted disposition recorded here and in the descending audit.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in deriving, checking and reviewing these findings. This is independent AI-assisted verification, not external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification. The unrestricted gap, prior results and external theorem dependencies are explicit. Merge only as a partial result: no preprint, Zenodo upload, DOI, tracker row or release is produced for this unsolved problem.\n\nAudit artifacts: draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr374_30005116 on main.\n","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:07:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T08:59:59Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f740e1740eeb39e4932bbcf295fdf2412a687f2f","assignees":[],"requested_revie